{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00151",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.58,
      "end_seconds": 5.49,
      "duration_seconds": 4.91,
      "text": "Uh, sorry I'm a few minutes behind, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 7.09,
      "end_seconds": 12.49,
      "duration_seconds": 5.4,
      "text": "So, no trouble at all, come in. What's been bothering you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 13.41,
      "end_seconds": 32.97,
      "duration_seconds": 19.56,
      "text": "Honestly, it's a fever for days, and my family pushed me to come. I wasn't sure whether to come in at all, to be honest. I kept putting it off, which I know isn't sensible."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 34.92,
      "end_seconds": 37.53,
      "duration_seconds": 2.61,
      "text": "when did you first notice it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 43.25,
      "end_seconds": 50.05,
      "duration_seconds": 6.8,
      "text": "it's been about two weeks now i did try to ignore it for a while"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 50.75,
      "end_seconds": 55.22,
      "duration_seconds": 4.47,
      "text": "Does it it happen all the time or in spells?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 56.47,
      "end_seconds": 59.04,
      "duration_seconds": 2.57,
      "text": "I'd say on and off."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 64.3,
      "end_seconds": 66.7,
      "duration_seconds": 2.4,
      "text": "how much is it bothering you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 67.22,
      "end_seconds": 68.15,
      "duration_seconds": 0.93,
      "text": "mostly severe"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 69.4,
      "end_seconds": 73.16,
      "duration_seconds": 3.76,
      "text": "Anything that tends to go along with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 74.93,
      "end_seconds": 86.88,
      "duration_seconds": 11.95,
      "text": "A bad headache goes along with it, most of the time. The bad headache? That's been for two days. I've also had constipation, since yesterday."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 100.47,
      "end_seconds": 107.03,
      "duration_seconds": 6.56,
      "text": "Right, any jaundice, blood in the stool, rash or burning when passing urine at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 107.98,
      "end_seconds": 109.69,
      "duration_seconds": 1.71,
      "text": "no, nothing there"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 110.97,
      "end_seconds": 112.23,
      "duration_seconds": 1.26,
      "text": "what about cough?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 114.31,
      "end_seconds": 115.77,
      "duration_seconds": 1.46,
      "text": "definitely no cough"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 116.28,
      "end_seconds": 120.69,
      "duration_seconds": 4.41,
      "text": "Ah. How about your heart, any problems like that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 121.72,
      "end_seconds": 126.54,
      "duration_seconds": 4.82,
      "text": "I mean, you know, no, nothing with my heart."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 127.07,
      "end_seconds": 129.28,
      "duration_seconds": 2.21,
      "text": "okay, any procedures or operations?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 130.87,
      "end_seconds": 135.36,
      "duration_seconds": 4.49,
      "text": "Just my tonsils out, when I was a child."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 136.35,
      "end_seconds": 140.48,
      "duration_seconds": 4.13,
      "text": "Anyone in the family with similar problems or other conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 142.28,
      "end_seconds": 144.42,
      "duration_seconds": 2.14,
      "text": "my brother has asthma"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 145.58,
      "end_seconds": 150.56,
      "duration_seconds": 4.98,
      "text": "Tell me about your health in general, any ongoing conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 151.21,
      "end_seconds": 153.57,
      "duration_seconds": 2.36,
      "text": "Diabetes, for nearly five years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 155.34,
      "end_seconds": 159.77,
      "duration_seconds": 4.43,
      "text": "Okay, I can see diabetes in your file as well."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 171.33,
      "end_seconds": 173.52,
      "duration_seconds": 2.19,
      "text": "What's your current medication list?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 174.46,
      "end_seconds": 184.62,
      "duration_seconds": 10.16,
      "text": "Glimepiride, 2 milligrams, before breakfast for my sugar. Dolo. I take it 650 milligrams, when I get the fever."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 185.35,
      "end_seconds": 188.26,
      "duration_seconds": 2.91,
      "text": "Now some background about your lifestyle."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 189.21,
      "end_seconds": 211.15,
      "duration_seconds": 21.94,
      "text": "I gave up drinking about three years ago. I used to smoke but I quit five years ago. I go to the gym a couple of times a week. Mostly home-cooked food, rice and vegetables. I work in an office, mostly sitting at a desk."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 212.92,
      "end_seconds": 216.26,
      "duration_seconds": 3.34,
      "text": "Before we go on, a few quick readings."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 230.13,
      "end_seconds": 231.1,
      "duration_seconds": 0.97,
      "text": "Almost there..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 247.52,
      "end_seconds": 257.74,
      "duration_seconds": 10.22,
      "text": "Okay: pulse 90, SpO2 98 percent on room air, BP is 122 over 69. And temperature 38.7, respiratory rate 18."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 259.56,
      "end_seconds": 263.04,
      "duration_seconds": 3.48,
      "text": "Is that alright, you know, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 264.77,
      "end_seconds": 267.4,
      "duration_seconds": 2.63,
      "text": "I'll explain what that means shortly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 269.05,
      "end_seconds": 272.42,
      "duration_seconds": 3.37,
      "text": "okay, I need to examine you for this"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 273.77,
      "end_seconds": 274.47,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "sure"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 275.59,
      "end_seconds": 277.88,
      "duration_seconds": 2.29,
      "text": "Almost done with this part."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 285.64,
      "end_seconds": 289.06,
      "duration_seconds": 3.42,
      "text": "I can't feel your liver or spleen enlarged."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 294.69,
      "end_seconds": 301.41,
      "duration_seconds": 6.72,
      "text": "Okay, finished. Putting it all together, I'd lean towards typhoid fever, which we need to confirm."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 302.39,
      "end_seconds": 305.16,
      "duration_seconds": 2.77,
      "text": "Is it something serious, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 307.01,
      "end_seconds": 321.58,
      "duration_seconds": 14.57,
      "text": "It's reasonable to be concerned, but right now typhoid fever, which we need to confirm is my leading thought, not anything worse. I think a full blood count makes sense here, for fever."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 322.4,
      "end_seconds": 325.01,
      "duration_seconds": 2.61,
      "text": "How long does that take?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 326.48,
      "end_seconds": 341.3,
      "duration_seconds": 14.82,
      "text": "I think blood cultures makes sense here, for prolonged fever. Eat only home-cooked food and drink boiled or bottled water while this is going on. Ask me anything before you go."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 342.2,
      "end_seconds": 345.29,
      "duration_seconds": 3.09,
      "text": "Thanks, um, that was helpful."
    }
  ]
}